{#
  Fleet summary for one patch run.

  Built by reading the per-host JSON files from the run directory rather than
  from hostvars, so that this template also renders a summary for a run that
  aborted part way through (see security-patch-summary.yml).
#}
{%- set run_dir = patch_report_dir ~ '/' ~ patch_run_id -%}
{%- set results = [] -%}
{%- for f in lookup('ansible.builtin.fileglob', run_dir ~ '/*.json', wantlist=True) | sort -%}
{%-   set _ = results.append(lookup('ansible.builtin.file', f) | from_json) -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- set failed      = results | selectattr('failed') | list -%}
{%- set rebooting   = results | selectattr('reboot_required') | list -%}
{%- set stale       = results | selectattr('stale_services') | list -%}
{%- set patched     = results | selectattr('changed_packages') | list -%}
{%- set clean       = results | rejectattr('changed_packages') | rejectattr('failed') | list -%}
{%- set skipped_exc = results | selectattr('excluded_with_pending_updates') | list -%}
# Security patch run `{{ patch_run_id }}`

Debian/Ubuntu fleet, security updates only. **This run did not reboot anything
and did not restart any services** — that is the fleet policy, so the follow-up
actions below are for a human to schedule.

## At a glance

| | Hosts |
|---|---|
| Reported | {{ results | length }} |
| Failed | {{ failed | length }} |
| Packages changed | {{ patched | length }} |
| Already up to date | {{ clean | length }} |
| **Reboot required** | **{{ rebooting | length }}** |
| Services running stale code | {{ stale | length }} |
| Excluded packages left vulnerable | {{ skipped_exc | length }} |

{% if failed %}
## Failed — investigate first

{% for r in failed %}
### `{{ r.host }}`

{{ r.failure | default('see the run log') }}

{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if rebooting %}
## Reboot required ({{ rebooting | length }})

Schedule a window for these. Until they reboot they are still running the
vulnerable kernel or libraries even though the new packages are installed.

| Host | OS | Running kernel | Requested by |
|---|---|---|---|
{% for r in rebooting %}
| `{{ r.host }}` | {{ r.distribution }} | {{ r.kernel }} | {{ r.reboot_packages | join(', ') if r.reboot_packages else 'unspecified' }} |
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if stale %}
## Services running pre-patch code ({{ stale | length }})

These picked up new shared libraries on disk but the running processes still map
the old ones. A service restart is enough; a reboot is not required.

| Host | Services |
|---|---|
{% for r in stale %}
| `{{ r.host }}` | {{ r.stale_services | join(', ') }} |
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if skipped_exc %}
## Deliberately left unpatched ({{ skipped_exc | length }})

These packages are in `patch_exclude_packages` and had a security update
available. Patch them by hand during a maintenance window.

| Host | Package | Installed | Available |
|---|---|---|---|
{% for r in skipped_exc %}
{% for pkg in r.excluded_with_pending_updates %}
| `{{ r.host }}` | `{{ pkg.name }}` | {{ pkg.current | default('-') }} | {{ pkg.candidate }} |
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

## Per host

| Host | Mode | Planned | Changed | Reboot | Result |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for r in results %}
| `{{ r.host }}` | {{ r.mode }} | {{ r.planned_upgrades | length + r.planned_new_packages | length }} | {{ r.changed_packages | length }} | {{ 'yes' if r.reboot_required else 'no' }} | {{ 'FAILED' if r.failed else 'ok' }} |
{% endfor %}

Per-host detail is in `{{ run_dir }}/<host>.md`.
